========================================================================
RESULT 3  the verdict on T5-T8
========================================================================
   T6 claims  sum(nu_i - 1) >= d - 1 :  1 >= 2 ?
  [PASS] T6 is REFUTED (the transitivity budget fails on a real etale non-injective map)
   T8 claims  r >= 2 :  r = 1
  [PASS] T8 is REFUTED (the non-properness set is irreducible here)

   WHY: pi_1 of the complement of an irreducible hypersurface is
   generated by the meridian AND ITS CONJUGATES.  Conjugate
   transpositions (12),(13) generate S_3 and act transitively on 3
   sheets, so one component with nu = 2 suffices.  T6 counted one
   generator per component; that is the error.
  [PASS] T5 and T7 are NOT tested here and remain unverified [DERIVED]

========================================================================
8/8 certifications passed.
========================================================================

GATE VERDICT: T6 and T8 REFUTED; T5 and T7 UNVERIFIED.

  Nothing may be built on T5-T8 as a family.  WP-2's congruence
  d = chi(C_L) mod 3 rests on T7, whose stablemates are now false and
  which was itself never verified - so WP-2 must not be run on this
  basis, and WP-5's "new handle" and WP-6 lose their support too.

  Per the handoff's decision tree this sends the session to WP-3, the
  GGHV (8,28) elimination, which depends on none of T5-T8.

  This is the gate doing exactly the job it was put there to do: the
  previous campaign's most expensive error was four sessions built on an
  unverified formula.  This one cost half a day.

